# Navigating Namma Metro: Bengaluru Metro Fare, Slabs, and Savings Guide (2026)

Navigating Bengaluru’s traffic can be a chaotic challenge. Thankfully, **Namma Metro** (Bengaluru Metro) serves as a fast, reliable, and air-conditioned savior for millions of commuters across the city.

However, following the implementation of the annual automatic fare revision by the Bangalore Metro Rail Corporation Limited (BMRCL), ticket prices across the 96-km operational network have undergone a slight change.

Whether you are a daily tech-corridor commuter or a tourist exploring the Garden City, this detailed guide breaks down the latest [**Bengaluru Metro**](https://metroguideindia.com/bengaluru-metro/) **fare** structure, active discount slabs, and includes an interactive cost calculator to help plan your commute budget perfectly.

## The New Bengaluru Metro Fare Structure (2026)

In compliance with the guidelines laid out by the First Fare Fixation Committee (FFC), BMRCL introduced a formula-based **annual automatic fare revision**. To insulate commuters from massive price shocks while keeping up with growing operational and electricity costs, the price adjustment has been strictly capped at **5%**.

As a result, ticket prices have marginally increased by ₹1 to ₹5 depending on the distance you travel. The **minimum fare is now ₹11** (up from ₹10), and the **maximum fare is ₹95** (up from ₹90).

### Official 2026 Fare Slabs by Distance

Namma Metro operates on an optimized 10-zone fare distance structure. Here is exactly what your token or base ticket costs:

| **Fare Zone** | **Distance Slab (Km)** | **Single Journey Token / Base Fare (INR)** |
| **F1** | 0 – 2 km | ₹11 |
| **F2** | 2 – 4 km | ₹21 |
| **F3** | 4 – 6 km | ₹32 |
| **F4** | 6 – 8 km | ₹42 |
| **F5** | 8 – 10 km | ₹53 |
| **F6** | 10 – 15 km | ₹63 |
| **F7** | 15 – 20 km | ₹74 |
| **F8** | 20 – 25 km | ₹84 |
| **F9 / F10** | Above 25 km | ₹95 |

## Smart Cards & NCMC: How to Slash Your Travel Costs

Even though the base ticket price has seen a marginal hike, BMRCL has retained all commuter-friendly discount metrics. If you use a **Contactless Smart Card** or a **National Common Mobility Card (NCMC)**, you can significantly lower your daily commute expenses.

> 💡 **Pro-Tip:** The minimum balance required to pass through the entry gates on a Namma Metro Smart Card is **₹90**. Keep your card topped up to avoid getting stopped at the turnstiles!

### 1. Time-Based Concessions

- **Peak Hours (5% Discount):** You automatically save 5% on the base fare when travelling during rush hours using your Smart card or NCMC.
- **Off-Peak Hours (10% Discount):** To encourage off-peak travel, BMRCL offers a generous 10% discount during the following windows on weekdays:
    - Start of service until **8:00 AM**
    - **12:00 PM** to **4:00 PM**
    - **9:00 PM** to closing time
- **Sundays & National Holidays (10% Discount):** Enjoy a flat 10% discount all day long on Sundays and designated national holidays (January 26, August 15, and October 2).

### 2. Tourist & Unlimited Day Passes

If you are exploring Bangalore or planning multiple trips in a single day, buying a standard token can quickly add up. You can opt for revised Tourist Passes available at station counters:

- **1-Day Pass:** ₹263 via Mobile QR / ₹313 via Smart Card (Offers unlimited travel for 24 hours).
- **3-Day Pass:** ₹578 via Mobile QR / ₹628 via Smart Card.
- **5-Day Pass:** ₹893 via Mobile QR / ₹943 via Smart Card.

## Interactive Bengaluru Metro Fare Calculator

Don't want to map out distances manually? Use our custom built, intuitive **Namma Metro Fare Calculator** below to estimate your exact trip cost for both tokens and smart cards instantly before stepping out!

