## Summary: Quick Tips for Your Next Journey

- **Ditch the Lines:** Skip the crowded ticket counter lines at busy hubs like Majestic (Nadaprabhu Kempegowda Station) or MG Road by purchasing digital QR tickets on the official Namma Metro mobile application or through WhatsApp.
- **Interchanges are Free:** You can switch lines (e.g., Purple Line to Green Line at Majestic, or the newly opening Yellow line intersections) without paying any extra transaction or exit fees, provided you don't exit the station gates.
- **Check the Clock:** If your travel time is flexible, try entering the station before 8:00 AM or between 12:00 PM and 4:00 PM to lock in the absolute cheapest 10% off-peak card discount!

## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) – Namma Metro Fares & Rules

### Q1: Is there a separate or discounted ticket fare for children in Namma Metro?

No, BMRCL does not charge fares based on age. Tickets are strictly based on **height**. Children under **3 feet (90 cm)** can travel completely free when accompanied by an adult. Anyone taller than 3 feet must purchase a full-fare ticket (token, QR code, or smart card).

### Q2: What is the minimum balance required on a Namma Metro Smart Card?

The minimum balance required to enter the automatic station gates using a Contactless Smart Card or NCMC is **₹90**. If your card balance falls below this limit, the turnstiles will not open, and you will need to top up your card at a counter or digital kiosk before entering.

### Q3: What is the maximum time limit allowed inside the metro station network?

Once you tap your ticket or card at the entry gate, you have a maximum of **120 minutes (2 hours)** to exit from any other station on the network. If you exceed this time limit, an overstay penalty fee of **₹10 per hour** (capped up to a maximum of ₹50) will be charged at the exit gate.

If you enter and exit from the _exact same station_, you must complete your turnaround within **20 minutes** to avoid paying a penalty.

### Q4: Are tokens valid for multiple days if left unused?

No. A Single Journey Token or digital QR code ticket is **only valid on the day of purchase**. Furthermore, after buying a physical token, you must tap into the entry gates within **30 minutes** at that specific station, or the token will expire and become invalid without a refund.

### Q5: Can I get a refund on an unused or partially used Metro Smart Card?

BMRCL does not offer refunds on the remaining travel balance loaded onto your Smart Card. However, the card itself comes with a massive **10-year validity** from the date of your last recharge, meaning your money stays safe for future trips if you take a break from commuting.

### Q6: Can I buy a single ticket or QR code for a group of people?

Yes! If you are traveling in a group, you can generate a **Group QR Ticket** via the official Namma Metro mobile app or WhatsApp. A single group QR code can accommodate up to **6 passengers** traveling together between the same two stations. Additionally, physical "Group Tickets" (paper tickets) are available at station counters for larger groups of 10 or more individuals at a discounted rate.
